      "writtenOn": "2026-10-12T12:05:21Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, the scenario you described is possible. The atomic flag was meant to be more of an optimization than a synchronization primitive and prevent from repeating the operations if the state would not change.\n\nTo make it thread-safe, we could use a reference counter instead of a flag, and lock interrupts with `irq_lock()` and `irq_unlock()` around the register accesses to prevent inconsistent hardware states.",
      "parentUuid": "992fadac_80cc105a",
      "revId": "78e0bae21a391309e4c28734d284fdecda4eaca8",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
